From: HarmonyOS Python Porting <porting@harmonyos.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Mar 2026 11:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] Modules/_posixsubprocess.c: Use /dev/fd on HarmonyOS

HarmonyOS does not provide /proc/self/fd but supports /dev/fd via
devfs, similar to FreeBSD and macOS. Add __OHOS__ to the FD_DIR
preprocessor condition so that /dev/fd is used on HarmonyOS for
file descriptor enumeration during subprocess fork/exec.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [HarmonyOS specific]
---
 Modules/_posixsubprocess.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Modules/_posixsubprocess.c b/Modules/_posixsubprocess.c
index xxxxxxxx..xxxxxxx 100644
--- a/Modules/_posixsubprocess.c
+++ b/Modules/_posixsubprocess.c
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
 # define readdir dirent64
 # endif
 #endif
 
-#if defined(__FreeBSD__) || (defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__MACH__)) || defined(__DragonFly__)
+#if defined(__FreeBSD__) || (defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__MACH__)) || defined(__DragonFly__) || defined(__OHOS__)
 # define FD_DIR "/dev/fd"
 #else
 # define FD_DIR "/proc/self/fd"
